**3. Brand Positioning**

━━━━━━━━━━

**Positioning Statement**

> *EDG Patio & Shade is the design and supply partner professionals
> trust for motorized pergolas, retractable screens, and glass enclosure
> systems. We work with builders, architects, designers, and dealers
> across the country---matching the right system to each project from
> multiple manufacturers, not pushing a single brand. Locally, we serve
> homeowners across the Chicago-Milwaukee corridor with full-service
> design, installation, and care. Wherever the project is, we bring the
> same thing: deep product knowledge, engineering support, and a team
> that actually picks up the phone.*

**What We Are**

-   The design and supply partner for professionals installing motorized
    outdoor systems---nationwide

-   Motorized pergola, screen, and glass enclosure specialists

-   System-agnostic (we recommend what's right, not what we're locked
    into)

-   Locally, full-service: design, supply, installation, and care plans
    from our own crews

-   A resource for trade partners---engineering support, system
    selection, training, and reliable execution

**What We Are NOT**

-   A deck builder who added pergolas to the menu

-   A single-brand dealer pushing one manufacturer

-   A generic "outdoor living" company

-   The cheapest option (we compete on knowledge, reliability, and
    execution---not price)

-   A local-only business (we design and supply nationally)

**Key Differentiators**

**1. We Own the Design/Supply Partner Niche**

Most motorized pergola and screen companies are set up to sell to
homeowners. We're built to support professionals. Builders, architects,
designers, and dealers come to us because we know the product landscape,
handle the engineering, and make their projects easier---whether they're
across town or across the country.

**2. System-Agnostic Expertise**

Most competitors are locked into one manufacturer (Erdmann = StruXure,
Warner's = Solace, OnDeck = Renson). We work with multiple manufacturers
and recommend what's right for each project. For trade partners, this
means we're specifying the best system for their client---not the one
we're contractually obligated to sell.

**3. National Reach, Local Roots**

We design and supply systems for professionals all around the country.
For projects in our home market---Lake County, McHenry County, the North
Shore, and Lake Geneva---we also install with our own crews. This dual
capability means trade partners get a single point of contact whether
they need design/supply only or a full turnkey solution.

**4. Specialization Over Generalization**

Motorized pergolas and screens are our core expertise, not an add-on to
a deck business. This matters for complex projects requiring
engineering, permitting, and integration with existing structures.

**5. Combined Pergola + Screen Expertise**

Screen-only companies don't do pergolas. Pergola companies treat screens
as an accessory. We own both categories under one roof---which means
trade partners only need one call, not two vendors.

**6. Physical Showroom**

Our Spring Grove showroom serves three purposes: a place for local
homeowners to see and touch products before buying, a resource for trade
partners to bring their clients, and a training facility for partner
installers. Most competitors don't have one.

